OL,3,GNEWSAPM open to giving Cornwall more
OL,4,Adevolved powers
OL,5,
OL,6,FPrime Minister Andy Burnham said he was
OL,7,Fopen to giving Cornwall Council and
OL,8,Fauthorities in other rural areas
OL,9,Fadvanced devolved powers previously
OL,10,Frestricted to mayors.
OL,12,FBurnham said he had spoken to the
OL,13,Fcounty's six MPs on a recent visit, and
OL,14,Fthey were "all in favour" and "very
OL,15,Fsupportive" of a devolution deal, with
OL,16,For without an elected mayor.
OL,18,FHe said local income tax retention, the
OL,19,Fmayoral Infrastructure Levy and the
OL,20,FStrategic Place Partnership - a higher
OL,21,Flevel scheme for housing - were "all on
OL,22,Fthe table for discussion".
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
